# Vitest 4's transform of a .mjs file with CRLF line endings fails with
# "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" on this project's toolchain
# (confirmed by direct bisection: byte-identical content differing only
# in line endings — LF passes, CRLF fails — when imported from a
# tests/containment/*.test.ts file). Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise silently convert a committed LF
# .mjs file back to CRLF on every checkout, intermittently breaking any
# test that imports one (see scripts/neon/cleanup-preview-branch.mjs
# and tests/containment/neonPreviewCleanup.test.ts). Force LF for these
# regardless of the checking-out machine's autocrlf setting.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
